WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.428 --> 00:00:04.251
Unit twenty-two. Two-Factor Authentication!

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:09.842
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emily, your technology teacher.

3
00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:12.784
Hi, Ms. Emily! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:17.037
Today we learn about Two-Factor Authentication. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:22.820
Two-factor. Say it with me. Two-factor!

6
00:00:26.306 --> 00:00:30.373
Password. Say it with me. Password!

7
00:00:33.879 --> 00:00:37.710
Code. Say it with me. Code!

8
00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:44.678
Phone. Say it with me. Phone!

9
00:00:48.196 --> 00:00:52.229
Account. Say it with me. Account!

10
00:00:55.736 --> 00:00:59.625
Login. Say it with me. Login!

11
00:01:03.082 --> 00:01:07.435
Security. Say it with me. Security!

12
00:01:10.985 --> 00:01:14.702
Hacker. Say it with me. Hacker!

13
00:01:18.135 --> 00:01:30.236
Two-factor authentication adds a second step to a login. After the password, you enter a code from your phone. Even if a hacker learns your password, your account stays safer.

14
00:01:30.286 --> 00:01:33.907
Now I understand. Thank you, Ms. Emily!

15
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:40.586
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:40.636 --> 00:01:41.786
Code!

17
00:01:42.785 --> 00:01:48.417
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:49.675
Security!

19
00:01:50.782 --> 00:01:57.763
Did you know? Turning on two-factor authentication blocks most automated attempts to break into accounts!

20
00:01:57.813 --> 00:02:00.080
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:01.188 --> 00:02:11.488
Think and answer. Why is two-factor authentication safer than a password alone?

22
00:02:11.538 --> 00:02:12.799
Great answer!

23
00:02:13.654 --> 00:02:19.891
Great job today! Keep learning, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:19.941 --> 00:02:22.946
Goodbye, everyone! See you next time!

